oof is\na rather simple consequence of a theorem of Zariski [KM98, Lemma 2.45], which does not\ndepend on this assumption.\nExample 1.21. Assume X is smooth, and let Z ⊂ X be a smooth irreducible subvariety.\nThe vanishing order at the generic point of Z is then a divisorial valuation ordZ ∈ X div ;\nindeed, denoting by π : X e → X the blowup of Z and E its exceptional divisor, we have\nordZ = ordE . Alternatively, ordZ = vP with P the exceptional divisor of the blowup X →\nXtriv of Z × {0}, i.e. the deformation to the normal cone of Z in X (see Example 1.7).\nRemark 1.22. The normalization X ν of a test configuration X for X is a test configuration\nfor the normalization X ν of X. The normalization morphism X ν → X factors through\nthe integral closure Xe, and the induced morphism X ν → Xe is an isomorphism over each\ngeneric point of Xe0 , Xe being regular at such points (compare [Oda13, Lemma 3.9]). As"
